    apart from the known board/.lock residue and .gitreins/history files).
    
    Re-verified at HEAD (commands run by this tick, not quoted from a prior artifact):
    CF-054 AC1 — the README Status-table line executed verbatim under env -i with a temp HOME
    exits rc=1 and prints "NODE: FAIL (3)", so the line carries the node check's status; the
    unreachable-URL row prints exactly one three-digit code ("-> 000"), so CF-037's fix holds.
    CF-055 AC1 — scripts/project-node.sh --check at HEAD printed 5 FAIL rows and
    "NODE: FAIL (5)", the two adapter-child rows included, so the parent counter matches.
    Section 14 and 15 fixtures of tests/selftest.sh cover both and are green.
    
    CF-070 — scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh:76-80 proves the inference layer with
    grep -qE '^[A-Z_]+_API_KEY=' and prints "PASS  inference_key — a provider key is present".
    An empty assignment (DEMO_API_KEY=) matches, so a keyless node is admitted on the layer
    whose own FAIL message says a turn dies at "No inference provider configured". Measured
    two-arm: empty value PASS, the same line commented out FAIL.
    
    CF-071 — the public-bind auth gate at install-hermes.sh:94 is grep -q 'basic_auth' against
    config.yaml, while the header promises --apply refuses a public bind without
    dashboard.basic_auth configured. A config whose only occurrence is commented out reaches
    the launch path; an empty config is refused. Measured two-arm with a hermetic hermes shim
    (same probe, arm A vs arm B), so the difference is exactly the gate's decision.
    
